 The pages under `docs/` are this repository's source of truth for people and coding agents. This page says which page
 owns each fact; read it before writing one.
+
+## Kinds and ownership
+
+- **[Features](features/README.md)** (explanation): current behavior of a unit of the app. Each page opens with who
+  needs it and why the behavior exists, describes its parts under subject-specific headings, and ends with
+  **Shaped by**, linking the decisions behind it. Behavior and configuration belong here; other pages link them.
+- **[Decisions](adrs/README.md)** (explanation): why a structural choice was made. Record a choice when reversing it
+  changes how the app's parts work together or imposes lasting operational constraints, and repository evidence
+  supplies the problem, alternatives and tradeoffs. Each record has a lead, then **Context**, **Options**,
+  **Decision**, and **Consequences**. Keep its number when the choice changes; update its title, slug and incoming
+  links, and preserve the earlier choice and why it changed in the reasoning.
+- **[Architecture](architecture.md)** (explanation): the current parts and their connections. Its lead sets scope;
+  **Parts** identifies components and **How they connect** describes connections. Link decisions for their reasons
+  and features for detailed behavior.
+- **[Runbooks](runbooks/README.md)** (how-to): actions for a concrete operational trigger. Each page has a lead naming
+  the reader, trigger, outcome and owner, then **Before you begin**, **Steps**, and **If it fails**. Each step states
+  the expected output so an operator can tell whether it worked.
+- **[Glossary](glossary.md)** (reference): shared terms and rejected synonyms. Each entry gives the preferred name,
+  its definition, and an **Avoid** list where needed.
+
+Each fact has one owning page by these criteria; other pages link to it. The guides in the directories list their
+pages. Code is evidence for current behavior; issue notes and version history supply the history and reasons to
+preserve on the owning page.
